# cmdline-ro.txt.fragment — Additions to /boot/firmware/cmdline.txt
#
# Add `ro` to the kernel command line to mount root read-only at boot.
# The image builder appends this to the existing cmdline.txt.
#
# If applying manually:
#   1. Mount the boot partition (vfat, /boot/firmware)
#   2. Edit cmdline.txt — it must be a single line with no newlines
#   3. Add `ro` after `rootwait`
#   4. Remove `fsck.repair=yes` if present (can't fsck a ro root at boot)
#
# Example transformation:
#
#   BEFORE:
#   console=serial0,115200 console=tty1 root=PARTUUID=... rootfstype=ext4 fsck.repair=yes rootwait quiet
#
#   AFTER:
#   console=serial0,115200 console=tty1 root=PARTUUID=... rootfstype=ext4 rootwait ro quiet
#
# NOTE: Do NOT use raspi-config overlay — it has a Bookworm bug that makes
#       all partitions read-only. The `ro` flag here only affects the root
#       filesystem (p2). /data (p4) remains read-write.
#
# The image builder uses sed to apply this:
#   sed -i 's/fsck\.repair=yes //g; s/rootwait/rootwait ro/' /boot/firmware/cmdline.txt

ro
